# Day 7 – Product Refinement & User Experience

## Overview

Day 7 focused on transforming the MVP into a polished, production-ready application. Rather than introducing major new functionality, the emphasis was on improving usability, visual design, responsiveness, accessibility, and overall user experience.

## Work Completed

### UI & UX Improvements

* Refined layouts and visual hierarchy
* Improved typography and spacing
* Enhanced responsive behaviour across devices
* Improved navigation and user flow
* Added polished loading, empty, and error states
* Increased accessibility and usability

### Product Polish

* Fixed UI inconsistencies
* Resolved bugs discovered during testing
* Improved application stability
* Optimized performance where possible
* Enhanced overall visual consistency

### Testing

* Verified existing features continue to function correctly
* Checked responsive layouts
* Validated user flows
* Reviewed edge cases and error handling

## Key Takeaway

Building features creates value.

Refining the experience creates products people enjoy using.

Today reinforced that successful software is not only functional—it is intuitive, accessible, reliable, and pleasant to interact with.

Moving into the final phase of the project with a stronger, cleaner, and more professional application.
